   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d50a044f-775f-4ad4-87ba-f9af0e40862d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We are using **Interquartile Range(IQR) Method**, which is a standard statistical technique for finding data points that fall significantly outside the central range of a dataset.\n",
    "    This is a way to find outliers- data point that are unsually high or low compared to the rest of the data- by focusing on the middle 50% of our data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b8e3fb67-b450-4a56-be55-a33ee78c2a5e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### **Replacing outliers with Boundaries**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
<<<<<<< Updated upstream
   "execution_count": 39,
=======
   "execution_count": null,
>>>>>>> Stashed changes
   "id": "fcdfd0be-e1de-4ba8-92e5-49e9845815a2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# These are the columns to check for outliers\n",
    "numeric_cols = [\n",
    "    'glucose',\n",
    "    'calories',\n",
    "    'heart_rate',\n",
    "    'steps',\n",
    "    'basal_rate',\n",
    "    'bolus_volume_delivered',\n",
    "    'carb_input'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# to finds the 25th percentil (Q1) and 75th percentile(Q3) for each health metric \n",
    "Q1 = merged_data[numeric_cols].quantile(0.25)\n",
    "Q3 = merged_data[numeric_cols].quantile(0.75)\n",
    "IQR = Q3 - Q1\n",
    "\n",
    "## Define the Upper and Lower Fences \n",
    "lower_fence =Q1 - 1.5 * IQR\n",
    "upper_fence = Q3 + 1.5 * IQR\n",
    "\n",
    "# Storing The Outlier's count before fixing\n",
    "outliers = (merged_data[numeric_cols] < (Q1 - 1.5 * IQR)) | \\\n",
    "           (merged_data[numeric_cols] > (Q3 + 1.5 * IQR))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Counts how many true values exist in each column, giving you a total outlier count for each metric.\n",
    "outliers.sum()\n",
    "\n",
    "# we create a copy to keep the original data safe\n",
    "df_cleaned = merged_data.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Apply clipping: values < lower fence become Q1, Values > Upper fence become Q3\n",
    "df_cleaned[numeric_cols] = df_cleaned[numeric_cols].clip(lower = lower_fence, upper = upper_fence, axis = 1)"
   ]
  },
